Description: Estimates habitat niche breadth corrected for the effects of
    abundance, using isodars (the relationships between a species' densities in
    pairs of habitats under density-dependent habitat selection). Fits pairwise
    and n-dimensional isodars, including data where sites lack some habitats,
    and computes the isodar-adjusted inequality (IAI) at any total abundance,
    with density-independent and density-dependent niche breadth, bootstrap
    confidence intervals and diagnostics. Method described in Granot, Dubiner and
    Belmaker (in revision, Ecology Letters).
